  "slug": "microbe-comprehensive-mapping-583d",
  "summary": "Database updates for MGnify v6, BGC Atlas v2, PhageScope 2.0, UHVDB and VEuPathDB land alongside new metaproteomics and 16S identification tools.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is large-scale reference resources for annotating microbial, viral and pathogen data, much of it from database updates. BGC Atlas v2 exceeds 16 million predicted biosynthetic gene clusters with taxonomic, environmental and geographic search. MGnify v6 adds amplicon variant analysis, broader viral and mobilome annotation, and Nextflow/Prefect automation. Viral coverage expands through PhageScope 2.0, a million-scale phage genomic, functional and structural resource, and UHVDB, an updateable set of 1.15 million clustered human-associated virus genomes with a profiling toolkit. VEuPathDB reports 2,602 datasets, AI-assisted curation and a PostgreSQL migration. In metaproteomics, Unipept supports multi-sample comparative projects with confidence scoring, while NovoTax builds sample-specific prokaryotic proteome databases from de novo MS sequencing rather than generic references. RADSuite targets species-level 16S resolution with a curated gene copy database and V-region detection. More peripheral are StarCrew for Starship cargo analysis and vartracker for longitudinal pathogen variant tracking.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-28"
}
